// This is a simple migration of a PNG image file to the assets directory
// No code conversion is needed as this is a binary file

// The file has been moved from:
// project-logo.png
// to:
// src/assets/images/project-logo.png

// In Angular, static assets like images should be placed in the assets folder
// which is configured in the angular.json file. This ensures they are properly
// copied during the build process.

// To reference this image in Angular templates, you would use:
// <img src="assets/images/project-logo.png" alt="Project Logo">

// Or in CSS/SCSS:
// background-image: url('/assets/images/project-logo.png');

// No TypeScript code is needed for this migration as it's just a file move operation.